| 52 | the library's `Vector` and `Matrix` carry a user element type in full, under `extends Number`: construction, indexing, `M v`, `v M`, `M N`, `.t()`, `+`, `scale`, `pmul`, `SUM`, comprehensions, mutation, runtime sizes | POSITIVE-VERIFIED | — | `Specification-1.0-frozen/basic/expressions/aggregate.tex:152-170`, "Array Expressions" | none | ours | `Number` has no `comprises` clause (P-160), so a program's type may extend it; the `Number` bound is the specification's own. Shown by a runtime-sized 3→4→2 forward pass over `Vector`/`Matrix` of a user `Value`, with ordinary `RR64` arithmetic still working alongside. Probe `explorations/libvector-probes/p30_capstone.fss`, in the parent of `e879b6a44`. |
